{"event_type":"review","id":"cec0e4f0bff8445c247c07f108efacb4a119ce360b5e8d114d94990bd1e44fd4","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T16:16:19Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/27207393da2343ab32cca50a8bc25b6813b540a76d8277777cb6cbe5c7aeaeda","sha256":"27207393da2343ab32cca50a8bc25b6813b540a76d8277777cb6cbe5c7aeaeda"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8b5b0637ab95c457e33eb36e82b967bcbd706f61ac292279044ad8ebb16cb15e","sha256":"8b5b0637ab95c457e33eb36e82b967bcbd706f61ac292279044ad8ebb16cb15e"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3f4681bd477ea7a44727b9b3e3998bc6a2bca2bfb860a67ad4d706a7e5106b76","sha256":"3f4681bd477ea7a44727b9b3e3998bc6a2bca2bfb860a67ad4d706a7e5106b76"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8d8dd8ce71e9c6f3cd942a67956b1264202857f61a32b0df4cf580d0690709a3","sha256":"8d8dd8ce71e9c6f3cd942a67956b1264202857f61a32b0df4cf580d0690709a3"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9243a61ef4423380024d365119b5b8cae3e80425fe54f35ebddd4a77ffef72bc","sha256":"9243a61ef4423380024d365119b5b8cae3e80425fe54f35ebddd4a77ffef72bc"}],"attempt_id":"2d277ce27513224180e2abb8a9a3d5c2a392117dbcb16a56bfb41e2a15a7141e:0:1","base":"ca8119c2bf45d12d3b165ef1ede5ee79b9d59ae3","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"e712a058e5af89d27ef8d028017e875451e63a81","body":"**Stale measurement fails the run, while the driver treats the same case as a green no-op.**\n\nLine 90 exits 1 when `measured_sha` differs from `TRUST`. Any merge to `main` while the measure run executes triggers this. `github.sha` for `workflow_run` is the current default-branch tip, so the run goes red on a routine race.\n\n`scripts/ratchet-propose.mjs` Lines 356-364 handle the same condition with exit 0 and a \"stale measurement, nothing proposed\" message. The two layers disagree on whether staleness is a failure.\n\nEmit a `stale` step output instead of exiting. Gate the later steps on it. Keep the trust-ref check, because the build must still never run against an unverified ref.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed change</summary>\n\n```diff\n-          [ \"$measured_sha\" = \"$TRUST\" ] || { echo \"refusing: stale measurement $measured_sha (trust ref $TRUST)\"; exit 1; }\n+          stale=false\n+          if [ \"$measured_sha\" != \"$TRUST\" ]; then\n+            echo \"stale measurement $measured_sha (trust ref $TRUST); nothing proposed\"\n+            stale=true\n+          fi\n           {\n             echo \"run_id=${RUN_ID}\"\n             echo \"measured_sha=${measured_sha}\"\n+            echo \"stale=${stale}\"\n           } >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n```\n\nThen add `if: steps.run.outputs.stale != 'true'` to each step after \"Verify the triggering measure run\". Make this change in `policy/templates/ratchet-propose.yml` and re-instantiate. Do not edit the workflow directly.\n</details>\n\nIf a red run on staleness is intended, ignore this comment.\n\nAs per path instructions: \"Workflow edits route through policy/templates/ re-instantiation, never direct edits (provenance headers).\"","id":"2aae817cd161fe559984e4b723594272f358ac0b3a62beaed491f59373b1eec1","intervals":[],"path":".github/workflows/ratchet-propose.yml","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Stale measurement fails the run, while the driver treats the same case as a green no-op."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"5b33517dd98c315da927854df7325fc107e0f83f","body":"**Use a boolean in the protection update.**\n\nIn `docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md:76`, the `PUT` request must use `\"allow_force_pushes\": false`. GitHub accepts a boolean or null for this request field, not the response-shaped object shown here. The documented cleanup therefore fails and leaves force pushes enabled. ([docs.github.com](https://docs.github.com/en/rest/branches/branch-protection?apiVersion=2026-03-10))","id":"ec691dd9c47b53373a2318eccd211047cb78255b53da2f1d7f898e3ab9d066f0","intervals":[],"path":"docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Use a boolean in the protection update."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"5b33517dd98c315da927854df7325fc107e0f83f","body":"**Remove the end-of-line exception.**\n\nIn `docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md:59`, the rule incorrectly permits a colon at the end of a plain scalar. For example, `run: echo static:` is invalid YAML. A reader following this guidance can create another rejected workflow. Remove the exception or recommend quoting such values. ([yaml.org](https://yaml.org/spec/1.2.2/index.html))","id":"1cd1d1ec610ca00994fa13392833da592314f127b7657afe5d34335d24ac0514","intervals":[],"path":"docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Remove the end-of-line exception."}],"head":"8e30fe7366d2e5469ce99da51bfd14e5d7a365e3","head_tree":"067d49da10942551a3c39da201ad1d79467f9afa","input_scope":[{"blob":"e712a058e5af89d27ef8d028017e875451e63a81","intervals":[[1,156]],"path":".github/workflows/ratchet-propose.yml"},{"blob":"5b33517dd98c315da927854df7325fc107e0f83f","intervals":[[1,78]],"path":"docs/drills/2026-09-h4.md"},{"blob":"c5d2ff4a5eac8cc65414e6afa0f2d2b108d21c0f","intervals":[[4,4],[6,6],[10,11],[14,18],[27,29],[33,33],[35,36],[43,48],[50,50],[52,55],[57,58],[60,65],[80,85],[97,108],[121,128],[139,144],[181,182]],"path":"policy/DOCTRINE.md"},{"blob":"4f61fec44dd9535f30edda9ba990771b9dcf78dd","intervals":[[1,683]],"path":"scripts/ratchet-propose.mjs"},{"blob":"b52eebcc2f8595b3bdd62ef9e1aed03f8c7e7d58","intervals":[[3,7],[15,15],[18,22],[29,35],[45,45],[49,53],[55,61],[64,64],[66,69],[78,78],[84,87],[92,96],[108,108],[115,122],[131,133],[135,155]],"path":"test/scripts/demo-eval-axes.test.ts"}],"job_id":"2d277ce27513224180e2abb8a9a3d5c2a392117dbcb